---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { OWNER_URL } from '../lib/rel';
---

<Base
  title="About webproxylist.org"
  description="Who runs webproxylist.org, how entries get here, and what inclusion does and does not mean."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1 style="margin-top:36px">About this directory</h1>

    <p>
      webproxylist.org is a directory of commercial proxy providers. Each entry is a single
      page covering protocols, geography, rotation, pricing and intended use, so that someone
      shopping for a provider can compare the things that actually differ between them.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      This site is operated by the team behind <a href={OWNER_URL}>ProxyVerity</a>, which
      publishes a free proxy list and a proxy checker. We say so here rather than leaving it
      to be discovered: the directory covers a market we also work in, and you should know
      that before you weigh anything on it.
    </p>

    <h2>How entries get here</h2>
    <p>
      Some entries are compiled by us from a provider's own public documentation and pricing
      pages. Others carry a description supplied by the provider; those pages say so directly
      above the text, every time. Nothing on this site is a paid review, and nothing here is
      ranked, scored or awarded a position.
    </p>
    <p>
      Inclusion is not an endorsement, and absence is not a judgement — it usually just means
      we have not written the page yet.
    </p>

    <h2>What the numbers are worth</h2>
    <p>
      Pricing, country coverage and feature lists come from the provider and change without
      notice. Treat every figure here as a starting point for your own check, not as a
      guarantee. Where a page states a date, that is when we last touched the entry.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you run one of the services listed and something is wrong or out of date, tell us and
      it gets fixed. Corrections do not require a relationship with us of any kind.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
